            <ArticleTitle>Unusual Presentation of Intrasacral Meningocele: A Case Report and Overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/jpn.JPN_124_16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intrasacral meningocele is an unusual congenital lesion. It is an intrathecal cystic formation arising as a protrusion of the arachnoid through a congenitally weak place in the dura mater. We report a case of a 12-year-old child with chronic pain with an intrasacral meningocele identified on magnetic resonance imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
